WEBVTT

00:00:39.850 --> 00:00:42.180
It's incredible!

00:02:18.910 --> 00:02:19.950
<i>April.</i>

00:02:20.700 --> 00:02:22.990
<i>It's a season of new beginnings.</i>

00:02:24.330 --> 00:02:26.160
Coming!

00:02:26.830 --> 00:02:30.080
<i>I'm in ninth grade now.</i>

00:02:32.210 --> 00:02:33.630
Hello.

00:02:34.250 --> 00:02:37.800
Machiko, right? Package from overseas.

00:02:39.930 --> 00:02:42.140
It's heavy!

00:02:42.470 --> 00:02:44.890
From Mom and Dad?

00:02:49.020 --> 00:02:51.600
They usually tell me when they're sending me something.

00:02:51.600 --> 00:02:52.650
I wonder what...

00:02:54.230 --> 00:02:57.240
Japanese rice... from overseas?

00:03:00.280 --> 00:03:01.320
Mom...

00:03:01.860 --> 00:03:08.080
You and Dad are so busy with work,
but you still went out of your way to...

00:03:11.170 --> 00:03:12.080
<i>That's right.</i>

00:03:12.080 --> 00:03:13.710
<i>I'll be taking my exams soon.</i>

00:03:13.710 --> 00:03:17.840
<i>I need to do well.</i>

00:03:19.760 --> 00:03:24.550
<i>I've got to make them proud!</i>

00:03:26.180 --> 00:03:28.730
I'm nervous about the test.

00:03:28.730 --> 00:03:32.400
They're going to grade us publicly, right?

00:03:33.020 --> 00:03:35.570
My hands won't stop shaking!

00:03:35.570 --> 00:03:37.110
Calm down.

00:03:37.110 --> 00:03:40.190
This test isn't that big of a deal.

00:03:40.190 --> 00:03:41.530
Right, Machiko?

00:03:43.780 --> 00:03:45.240
<i>I can do this!</i>

00:03:46.200 --> 00:03:49.370
Okay, let's begin the practical test.

00:03:49.790 --> 00:03:51.910
This motif...

00:03:51.910 --> 00:03:56.630
Your subject is a still life sketch of the motif on the table.

00:03:56.630 --> 00:03:57.750
All right, begin.

00:04:07.350 --> 00:04:11.140
<i>I can't think of anything but rice with bamboo shoots.</i>

00:04:13.100 --> 00:04:16.110
<i>How am I going to do this?</i>

00:04:16.110 --> 00:04:17.940
<i>I don't know, but first...</i>

00:04:21.530 --> 00:04:22.860
<i>I can do this!</i>

00:04:22.860 --> 00:04:25.530
Please keep quiet during the test.

00:04:27.910 --> 00:04:30.080
All right, we're done with the feedback.

00:04:30.080 --> 00:04:33.540
I'm sure you all now have a clearer understanding of what your strong points are,

00:04:33.540 --> 00:04:36.080
and what you'll need to focus on.

00:04:36.960 --> 00:04:38.920
This sucks.

00:04:38.920 --> 00:04:39.170
I dunno, I think it works.

00:04:40.550 --> 00:04:41.380
How'd you do, Ryo?

00:04:41.380 --> 00:04:44.510
I almost made the top ten in my class!

00:04:44.880 --> 00:04:46.390
Third.

00:04:46.390 --> 00:04:48.850
Third? That's awesome!

00:04:48.850 --> 00:04:50.640
I knew you were a good artist!

00:04:50.970 --> 00:04:53.430
Third from last...

00:04:54.190 --> 00:04:55.100
From last?!

00:04:55.100 --> 00:04:58.060
Wait, what happened to your face?

00:04:58.060 --> 00:04:59.650
I tried to fire myself up.

00:04:59.650 --> 00:05:01.030
You what?

00:05:01.030 --> 00:05:04.150
And I didn't sketch the assigned subject.

00:05:04.150 --> 00:05:05.320
That's...

00:05:06.950 --> 00:05:09.200
Definitely not a still life!

00:05:09.910 --> 00:05:13.120
The motif looked so tasty that I got caught up in the moment

00:05:13.500 --> 00:05:15.920
and just couldn't stop myself.

00:05:16.370 --> 00:05:19.670
<i>Mmm... bamboo shoots...</i>

00:05:19.670 --> 00:05:21.420
<i>So springy!</i>

00:05:21.960 --> 00:05:25.880
I don't want to tell my parents how badly I did.

00:05:25.880 --> 00:05:28.590
It's a new semester, and I'm already so worried.

00:05:29.220 --> 00:05:30.430
Ryo...

00:05:30.430 --> 00:05:34.930
D-Don't worry! You may have gotten the subject wrong, but it still looks great!

00:05:34.930 --> 00:05:38.690
Like the crunchy bamboo shoots, the fluffy rice...

00:05:38.690 --> 00:05:39.860
Fluffy...

00:05:42.150 --> 00:05:44.820
Let's have rice with bamboo shoots tonight, Ryo!

00:05:44.820 --> 00:05:47.780
Looking at that sketch has given me a craving!

00:05:47.780 --> 00:05:49.570
Um....

00:05:51.990 --> 00:05:54.000
Let me get my bag.

00:05:54.000 --> 00:05:55.080
'Kay.

00:05:59.790 --> 00:06:00.590
Sir!

00:06:05.550 --> 00:06:06.220
Shiina!

00:06:08.720 --> 00:06:10.890
Did you need something, Morino?

00:06:10.890 --> 00:06:13.100
Are you pretending to be a captured Roswell Grey?

00:06:14.060 --> 00:06:16.350
No way!

00:06:18.690 --> 00:06:22.150
Are you sure we're allowed to take all of these?

00:06:22.150 --> 00:06:25.150
He said they were done with them anyway.

00:06:25.150 --> 00:06:28.860
Plus, I'm sure the ingredients are happy they get to be cooked by you.

00:06:28.860 --> 00:06:30.870
Well...

00:06:32.070 --> 00:06:33.240
Oh, shoot!

00:06:38.000 --> 00:06:39.040
Here!

00:06:39.710 --> 00:06:41.290
Thanks.

00:06:41.290 --> 00:06:43.130
Wait, is that you, Shiina?

00:06:43.130 --> 00:06:45.760
How long have you been here?

00:06:45.760 --> 00:06:46.630
The whole time.

00:06:48.170 --> 00:06:51.930
Well, we've been walking together since we left school.

00:06:51.930 --> 00:06:53.760
Or so it seems.

00:06:54.390 --> 00:06:57.680
Sorry, I'm being such an airhead today!

00:06:58.020 --> 00:06:59.440
Don't worry about it, Shiina.

00:07:02.980 --> 00:07:07.070
Don't you live in the other direction? What's up?

00:07:07.940 --> 00:07:10.820
You don't know? Morino invited—

00:07:13.450 --> 00:07:15.660
She said you were feeling down and—

00:07:19.160 --> 00:07:20.750
Shh! Don't tell!

00:07:20.750 --> 00:07:23.790
Why? I thought we were trying to cheer her up?

00:07:23.790 --> 00:07:26.710
Yeah, but we gotta do it casually!

00:07:26.710 --> 00:07:27.420
Kirin?

00:07:28.170 --> 00:07:31.130
Shiina says she'll be abducted by aliens

00:07:31.130 --> 00:07:33.260
if she doesn't eat rice with bamboo shoots today!

00:07:33.260 --> 00:07:37.180
See? Nothing abnormal going on!

00:07:37.970 --> 00:07:39.680
Sounds abnormal to me.

00:07:39.680 --> 00:07:42.400
Aliens?

00:07:45.440 --> 00:07:48.780
First, let's blanch the shoots.

00:07:48.780 --> 00:07:50.440
Blanch?

00:07:52.780 --> 00:07:57.870
Bamboo shoots get astringent after harvest,

00:07:57.870 --> 00:08:02.960
so they need to be prepared by boiling them with rice bran for an hour.

00:08:06.210 --> 00:08:08.460
Ick, that's bitter!

00:08:08.750 --> 00:08:11.590
It's not good if they're allowed to grow too long either.

00:08:11.590 --> 00:08:13.840
Ugh, too hard!

00:08:13.840 --> 00:08:17.470
Kirin, you can't just go putting everything in your mouth!

00:08:17.470 --> 00:08:23.230
But my favorite picture book showed people eating long shoots!

00:08:23.230 --> 00:08:25.650
Picture books are just made up.

00:08:25.650 --> 00:08:28.400
Though you're right, they do look tasty.

00:08:28.400 --> 00:08:30.740
Yeah, I can see why.

00:08:30.740 --> 00:08:32.990
Like, food in comics and on TV?

00:08:34.490 --> 00:08:38.490
Don't you think they always seem really good for some reason?

00:08:38.490 --> 00:08:43.580
Like steak in comics, or those huge pancakes, or soccer rice balls.

00:08:43.910 --> 00:08:45.790
You're right!

00:08:45.790 --> 00:08:49.750
But when you try to make it yourself, it never quite works.

00:08:52.470 --> 00:08:55.300
Soft-cooked rice omelettes sound good too.

00:08:55.300 --> 00:08:56.430
Rice omelettes!

00:08:56.800 --> 00:09:00.180
You mean, like, "From the Eggpennines to the White Peaks"?

00:09:00.180 --> 00:09:02.020
You watched that too?

00:09:02.020 --> 00:09:04.730
The one starring the laid-off office worker, right?

00:09:04.730 --> 00:09:08.560
He collapses and is saved by a restaurateur he doesn't recognize!

00:09:08.560 --> 00:09:11.860
Even though he only had their rice
omelettes once, he'll never forget it!

00:09:12.360 --> 00:09:15.110
That must be where we all heard of...

00:09:15.990 --> 00:09:18.490
The legendary soft-cooked rice omelettes!

00:09:19.990 --> 00:09:24.250
When you cut into the omelette,
the egg just comes oozing out...

00:09:25.500 --> 00:09:27.500
I'd love to try that!

00:09:27.500 --> 00:09:31.880
I tried making it with a single egg a long time ago, but it came out terribly.

00:09:31.880 --> 00:09:35.970
Of course, that's nowhere near enough egg to cover the rice.

00:09:37.010 --> 00:09:40.430
Just talking about it makes me hungry.

00:09:40.430 --> 00:09:42.010
Are the rice and bamboo shoots done yet?

00:09:44.020 --> 00:09:46.230
Should be soon!

00:09:47.850 --> 00:09:51.860
It feels like we're opening a treasure chest!

00:09:51.860 --> 00:09:52.980
Here goes.

00:10:04.950 --> 00:10:07.040
Oh my God, it just looks too good!

00:10:07.040 --> 00:10:09.960
The rice looks like it's dancing with excitement!

00:10:12.960 --> 00:10:13.590
Well, then.

00:10:14.090 --> 00:10:15.630
Let's eat!

00:10:24.180 --> 00:10:26.640
It's super soft and has the perfect mix of sweet and salty!

00:10:28.600 --> 00:10:31.980
I can't resist the power of the bamboo shoot!

00:10:34.820 --> 00:10:37.150
I love the scorched rice.

00:10:39.160 --> 00:10:44.240
The well-done shoots and the rich fried flavor...

00:10:44.240 --> 00:10:47.160
I could chew on them all day.

00:10:56.300 --> 00:10:58.840
The firm texture...

00:10:58.840 --> 00:11:01.390
The distinct flavor that just
melts in your mouth...

00:11:01.390 --> 00:11:03.680
It's so delicate and nostalgic.

00:11:03.680 --> 00:11:06.930
It's amazing how well the bamboo shoots go with the rice.

00:11:06.930 --> 00:11:10.940
You look so dainty when you're eating, Shiina.

00:11:11.230 --> 00:11:14.190
It's so mature, but in a different way than usual.

00:11:14.650 --> 00:11:16.650
Anyway, seconds please!

00:11:18.820 --> 00:11:20.400
I'll get it.

00:11:20.700 --> 00:11:23.160
Th-Thanks.

00:11:33.040 --> 00:11:35.960
Here you go. A heaping bowl of rice, just like in the comics.

00:11:37.800 --> 00:11:39.590
I'll fill yours too, Machiko.

00:11:41.800 --> 00:11:48.560
<i>Now that I think of it, it's been a long time since anyone's served me food like this.</i>

00:11:51.100 --> 00:11:55.060
Thank you so much! I've always wanted to try it like this!

00:11:58.230 --> 00:12:01.490
<i>I feel really comfy tonight.</i>

00:12:02.150 --> 00:12:05.820
<i>I guess it's because we're all sitting around the table like family.</i>

00:12:07.830 --> 00:12:10.200
Finish your carrots, Morino.

00:12:10.200 --> 00:12:12.210
H-How'd you know I wasn't gonna?!

00:12:12.580 --> 00:12:16.960
<i>I was so stressed out because of how I did on my test,</i>

00:12:16.960 --> 00:12:20.210
<i>but being with them makes me relax.</i>

00:12:29.560 --> 00:12:31.230
That was great.

00:12:33.520 --> 00:12:35.230
There's still a little left.

00:12:35.230 --> 00:12:38.690
That's okay. I can make rice balls with it.

00:12:38.690 --> 00:12:40.280
It's getting pretty late.

00:12:40.280 --> 00:12:43.110
Would you like to stay over, Shiina?

00:12:43.110 --> 00:12:44.570
I can call your parents.

00:12:44.860 --> 00:12:46.200
Are you sure?

00:12:47.320 --> 00:12:49.450
It's fine, I guess.

00:12:49.450 --> 00:12:53.210
Tomorrow is a holiday, so Kirin's staying over too.

00:12:53.210 --> 00:12:54.460
Plus...

00:12:54.830 --> 00:12:58.710
Aren't those aliens still after you?

00:12:58.710 --> 00:13:02.550
I'm worried about you walking home alone.

00:13:04.130 --> 00:13:07.970
Don't worry, though. I won't tell anyone.

00:13:07.970 --> 00:13:09.680
<i>She actually believed it?!</i>

00:13:09.680 --> 00:13:11.140
<i>She's </i>too<i> nice.</i>

00:13:21.820 --> 00:13:26.410
Wow, it's "From the Eggpennines to the White Peaks"!
I haven't seen this in forever!

00:13:26.410 --> 00:13:29.410
I forgot he was in it.

00:13:29.410 --> 00:13:30.950
Here it comes.

00:13:34.410 --> 00:13:36.290
I'm so happy.

00:13:36.290 --> 00:13:40.920
I'm happiest while eating rice omelettes!

00:13:42.050 --> 00:13:43.960
There it is! His catchphrase!

00:13:43.960 --> 00:13:46.010
That brings it all together.

00:13:46.010 --> 00:13:47.970
I can really feel where he's coming from.

00:13:47.970 --> 00:13:51.060
Rice omelettes are so tender and gentle.

00:13:51.470 --> 00:13:54.270
That could very well be the taste of happiness.

00:13:54.890 --> 00:13:57.520
The taste of happiness?

00:14:07.400 --> 00:14:09.620
Oh no, I must have fallen asleep.

00:14:11.160 --> 00:14:12.030
Huh?

00:14:12.580 --> 00:14:14.790
Kirin? Shiina?

00:14:14.790 --> 00:14:17.290
Have they gone home?

00:14:18.620 --> 00:14:22.170
It must be because I drifted off.

00:14:22.170 --> 00:14:24.420
I hope they're not mad.

00:14:24.920 --> 00:14:27.670
<i>I see this every day, and yet...</i>

00:14:36.810 --> 00:14:38.350
We're back, Ryo!

00:14:38.850 --> 00:14:40.600
Sorry, we borrowed your keys.

00:14:40.600 --> 00:14:42.650
Where did you two...

00:14:43.940 --> 00:14:45.030
Let's have some...

00:14:45.030 --> 00:14:46.820
...rice omelettes!

00:14:50.490 --> 00:14:53.280
You went shopping instead of going to sleep?

00:14:53.280 --> 00:14:58.040
My appetite conquered my drowsiness.

00:14:58.040 --> 00:15:01.790
I absolutely have to have some rice omelettes,

00:15:01.790 --> 00:15:03.960
so I'm having you two make it.

00:15:04.710 --> 00:15:05.960
That's nice.

00:15:05.960 --> 00:15:07.050
No, it's not!

00:15:07.050 --> 00:15:10.800
I've had that show's rice omelettes floating in front of my eyes all night!

00:15:10.800 --> 00:15:12.300
Save me, Ryo!

00:15:12.800 --> 00:15:14.140
Okay.

00:15:18.850 --> 00:15:20.140
You're fast!

00:15:23.150 --> 00:15:25.690
Wow, that's a lot of rice!

00:15:25.690 --> 00:15:30.610
Yep, I boiled a lot of the rice my parents sent me.

00:15:30.610 --> 00:15:32.950
I mixed in a good deal of ingredients too.

00:15:33.700 --> 00:15:35.990
It'll be like a top 40 countdown of rice omelettes!

00:15:35.990 --> 00:15:37.450
Yay!

00:15:39.830 --> 00:15:44.290
First up, we have just good old fashioned rice omelettes!

00:15:47.550 --> 00:15:51.970
That puffy shape is still amazing, no matter how old you are!

00:15:52.430 --> 00:15:54.720
Ketchup's for more than just writing something, it adds—

00:15:58.930 --> 00:16:00.310
A dying message?

00:16:00.770 --> 00:16:04.270
All I care about is its taste!

00:16:09.650 --> 00:16:13.360
The messy ketchup rice is great!

00:16:15.530 --> 00:16:18.040
Next, it's time for a change.

00:16:18.040 --> 00:16:20.120
Okonomiyaki-style rice omelettes!

00:16:22.870 --> 00:16:25.380
That looks like the kind of rice omelettes they'd make in Kansai.

00:16:26.380 --> 00:16:30.380
Wonder if it'll give her a Kansai accent?

00:16:31.880 --> 00:16:33.050
That would be wonderful.

00:16:42.270 --> 00:16:43.940
Um...

00:16:44.560 --> 00:16:49.070
Yo, dat thick spicy mayo is a perfect match!

00:16:50.320 --> 00:16:54.400
Change-up? This be more like a level-up!

00:16:54.400 --> 00:16:55.320
Good job.

00:16:55.950 --> 00:17:02.250
This one has a thick Japanese-style broth.

00:17:03.910 --> 00:17:06.250
I call it "springtime rice omelettes."

00:17:09.130 --> 00:17:11.460
The aroma of spring is wafting off it!

00:17:11.460 --> 00:17:13.720
It makes me glad I'm Japanese!

00:17:13.720 --> 00:17:16.340
You're one heck of a meal recycler, Ryo.

00:17:16.680 --> 00:17:18.800
You're the queen of leftovers!

00:17:19.180 --> 00:17:23.310
I don't think I like either of those nicknames...

00:17:30.070 --> 00:17:31.900
Doria-style rice omelettes...

00:17:31.900 --> 00:17:34.650
The stringy cheese is delectable.

00:17:38.320 --> 00:17:40.450
The Chinese-style is delish too!

00:17:40.450 --> 00:17:45.040
I could keep eating the sweet-and-sour ketchup base forever!

00:17:54.300 --> 00:17:57.800
Ryo, take a break and come have some!

00:17:58.090 --> 00:18:02.810
But if I don't get the legendary
soft-cooked rice omelettes right...

00:18:04.810 --> 00:18:07.140
Huh? This one looks fine.

00:18:07.140 --> 00:18:09.610
Not quite. I'm going to try again.

00:18:09.610 --> 00:18:12.270
How about if you put a soft omelette on top?

00:18:12.270 --> 00:18:16.190
No. It has to open at the top and let the egg flow out.

00:18:26.910 --> 00:18:27.790
There!

00:18:28.290 --> 00:18:29.040
Here!

00:18:33.550 --> 00:18:35.050
Here I go.

00:18:42.300 --> 00:18:44.640
I... I...

00:18:44.640 --> 00:18:46.930
I did it!

00:18:46.930 --> 00:18:48.310
It's a work of art.

00:18:57.240 --> 00:18:59.950
It's incredible!

00:19:00.320 --> 00:19:02.740
The smooth feel of the egg on my tongue,

00:19:02.740 --> 00:19:06.240
and the thick, rich sauce filling my mouth.

00:19:06.240 --> 00:19:11.330
The sourness of the ketchup rice and the creaminess of the eggs blends so well.

00:19:12.540 --> 00:19:13.790
I love it.

00:19:15.250 --> 00:19:17.340
The ones you messed up are also awesome!

00:19:17.670 --> 00:19:20.050
I'm so happy.

00:19:21.130 --> 00:19:23.890
I said the line from the show.

00:19:25.100 --> 00:19:27.270
Really? Are you really happy?!

00:19:29.230 --> 00:19:30.230
Yes.

00:19:33.560 --> 00:19:39.490
Machiko, is there anything else you've seen that you'd like to try? In comics, or on TV?

00:19:39.820 --> 00:19:42.200
Hmm, let's see...

00:19:42.200 --> 00:19:47.740
How about something rich and fatty like really gooey grilled cheese?

00:19:47.740 --> 00:19:50.080
I wanna try that too!

00:19:50.080 --> 00:19:51.750
Steak's a good idea too!

00:19:51.750 --> 00:19:52.580
Sounds good.

00:19:52.580 --> 00:19:55.040
Why don't we try them together?

00:19:55.040 --> 00:19:56.420
Yeah!

00:20:00.010 --> 00:20:01.840
I'll make some tea.

00:20:02.340 --> 00:20:03.680
Thanks.

00:20:11.140 --> 00:20:15.730
We've already gone through a lot of the rice.

00:20:15.730 --> 00:20:18.320
Thanks, Mom.

00:20:26.620 --> 00:20:29.160
Good friends...

00:20:29.410 --> 00:20:32.830
<i>When I talk to Mom and Dad...</i>

00:20:32.830 --> 00:20:34.920
<i>I don't want to just talk about my grades.</i>

00:20:35.330 --> 00:20:40.130
<i>I want to tell them all about Kirin and Shiina too.</i>

00:20:41.340 --> 00:20:43.340
So I guess me staying over worked out?

00:20:44.090 --> 00:20:46.390
I mean, we don't get many days off.

00:20:46.390 --> 00:20:49.100
I figured you'd rather spend the day alone with Machiko.

00:20:49.100 --> 00:20:53.940
It was my idea to begin with, and Ryo looked like she had more fun with the three of us.

00:20:54.560 --> 00:20:58.320
I kinda like how cheerful it is with another person here too.

00:21:02.320 --> 00:21:06.570
Hardly surprising. It's impossible to not have fun when I'm around.

00:21:06.870 --> 00:21:08.700
Where'd you get that idea from?

00:21:14.210 --> 00:21:18.250
Hey, that's the theme song to "From the Eggpennines to the White Peaks"!

00:21:26.760 --> 00:21:28.760
Thanks for walking me to the station.

00:21:31.970 --> 00:21:35.770
You two had better not sneak off for some cake on your way back!

00:21:36.440 --> 00:21:39.520
You can still eat after all we've had?

00:21:40.070 --> 00:21:41.780
See you next week!

00:21:42.150 --> 00:21:43.570
Yeah.

00:21:49.780 --> 00:21:52.040
You know what? Let's go get some pancakes.

00:21:53.540 --> 00:21:55.250
That should be fine, right?

00:21:55.250 --> 00:21:58.080
I mean, they're not really a cake,

00:21:58.080 --> 00:22:00.840
so we're technically not cheating on her.

00:22:00.840 --> 00:22:02.840
Ch-Cheating?

00:22:03.710 --> 00:22:05.090
Hold on, I've got a text.

00:23:41.980 --> 00:23:45.730
I'm not really good at wrapping the ones that go in plastic.

00:23:45.730 --> 00:23:48.820
I always end up tearing the seaweed.

00:23:48.820 --> 00:23:54.030
Think of it like you're wrapping a black blanket around the white rice.

00:23:54.030 --> 00:23:57.490
See? With a little face peeking out.

00:23:57.490 --> 00:24:00.790
Now wrap the blanket around here too.

00:24:01.750 --> 00:24:04.380
Ryo, that's kind of scary.

00:24:04.380 --> 00:24:06.750
Next on Gourmet Girl Graffiti!

00:24:06.750 --> 00:24:08.760
Moist and Crispy!
